[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3636596772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113836#issuecomment-3636596772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113836","id":3636596772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YwhAk","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T11:17:43Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T11:17:43Z","body":"Do you have some examples of cases where this would be needed? Enums to use for binding should be clearly named so I'm not sure the `enum class` syntax is *needed*, and adding a new macro for a hypothetical but adding complexity and extra macros to keep track of should be justified IMO","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3636596772/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3636890283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113836#issuecomment-3636890283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113836","id":3636890283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Yxoqr","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T12:33:34Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T12:34:09Z","body":"> In theory we could update the old enum but I wanted to suggest an addition rather than a breaking change. The only case I can think that updating the old define could cause issues is if people were depending on it for checking.\r\n\r\nWhy would changing the old enum be a breaking change?\r\nI would prefer if we change the old enum instead of adding a new one.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3636890283/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637561359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113836#issuecomment-3637561359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113836","id":3637561359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Y0MgP","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-10T15:11:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T15:11:19Z","body":"The overall idea of allowing the binding of enum classes makes sense to me! But I agree with @Ivorforce that we should update the original macro, rather than adding a new one","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3637561359/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3641185388","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113836#issuecomment-3641185388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113836","id":3641185388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZCBRs","user":{"login":"Kimau","id":905911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTkxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/905911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau","html_url":"https://github.com/Kimau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T10:07:12Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T10:07:12Z","body":"I'm all for updating the original that is what I did in my branch. I was just concerned about a few very minor corner cases:\r\n\r\n**Large Unsigned Values**: Values in unsigned enums (e.g., uint32_t flags > INT_MAX) are cast correctly to int64_t without unwanted sign extension or value mangling, which static_cast handles but implicit conversion sometimes handles differently.\r\n\r\n**Compiler Warnings**: Whether enforcing static_cast on everything might trigger \"useless cast\" warnings on some strict compiler configurations for standard int enums.\r\n\r\nI'll make a version updating og macro now","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3641185388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643634605","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113836#issuecomment-3643634605","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113836","id":3643634605,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZLXOt","user":{"login":"Kimau","id":905911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTkxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/905911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau","html_url":"https://github.com/Kimau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kimau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T20:18:53Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T20:18:53Z","body":"Yeah sadly this was something I needed expanded to extensions because of horrid build times we have some code that alternates between Extension or Module depending on build type. We resolved the name scope issue with\r\n```cpp\r\n\t{\r\n\t\tusing enum MoveJustMade;\r\n\t\tBIND_ENUM_CONSTANT(MJM_UNKNOWN)\r\n\t\tBIND_ENUM_CONSTANT(MJM_GOOD)\r\n\t\tBIND_ENUM_CONSTANT(MJM_UNDO)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThough it would be nice to actually have a decent macro that binds and scopes the enum nicely in a more nested way.\r\nAtm I'm head down on deadlines and honestly this was just an annoyance I changed in our version of the engine I though I would flow back to main.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3643634605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]